<!--
  To use these in a stage:

  1) Set stage string key value 'initial_lighting_setup_id' with flag PERSISTENT to any of the setup ids like 'INITIAL_UNDERGROUND'.
  2) Set stage string key value 'current_lighting_setup_id' with flags PERSISTENT and SAVE_STATE to any of the setup ids like 'INITIAL_UNDERGROUND'.
     This is required so that the current light setup is saved with the save game.
  3) Set stage persistent boolean key value 'simulate_time_of_day' to false.
  4) Add marker with template type LIGHTING_SETUP to the stage:
    -It calls Game_SetWorldLightingSetup when the player enters the marker area, and
    -calls Game_RevertWorldLightingSetup when the player leaves the marker area.

  This file is automatically reloaded when the game starts and developer mode is enabled.
-->
